From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mingyu Lei <leimy@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 08:50:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] [M156] FSA: disallow platform path resolution in
 incognito

Original change's description:
> FSA: disallow platform path resolution in incognito
>
> Off-the-record FileSystemContext instances store sandboxed files in
> memory via `ObfuscatedFileUtilMemoryDelegate`, but still construct
> synthetic paths rooted under the parent profile directory. Resolving a
> platform path for an incognito entry therefore does not correspond to an
> in-memory backing file and can collide with an on-disk file in the
> regular profile, causing DoGetPlatformPath to grant
> `ChildProcessSecurityPolicy` read access to that physical path.
>
> Make `FileSystemOperationImpl::SyncGetPlatformPath()` reject incognito
> contexts with `FILE_ERROR_INVALID_OPERATION` and propagate
> GetLocalFilePath errors instead of unconditionally returning `FILE_OK`.
> Also check both `context->is_incognito()` and the `SyncGetPlatformPath`
> result in `GetPlatformPathOnFileThread` before granting read access on
> the UI thread.
>
> In the follow up CL, we are proposing to remove the API, but the current
> one will be landed first and ideally cherry picked into previous
> milestones to fix the vulnerability.
>
